# This repository lives at the root of a Windows user profile, which
# contains many sensitive files by nature (SSH keys, passwords, VPN/RDP
# certificates, network configs, etc.). Rather than trying to enumerate
# every sensitive file/pattern (new ones will keep appearing here), this
# .gitignore uses an ALLOWLIST strategy: everything is ignored by default,
# and only specific, intentional documentation files are allowed in.
#
# To track a new file in this repo, add an explicit "!" rule for it below.
# Do NOT switch this to a denylist approach in this directory.

# Ignore everything by default.
*

# Never ignore this file itself.
!.gitignore

# Allow the Documents directory to be traversed...
!/Documents/

# ...but only allow specific known-safe files within it.
!/Documents/spicylabs-mail-troubleshooting-README.md

# Explicitly called out for clarity (already covered by the default-deny
# above, listed here just to document what must NEVER be tracked):
# - .ssh/                          (private keys)
# - AppData/                       (app data, caches, credentials)
# - Documents/*.txt, Documents/*.rdp   (passwords, PSKs, IP configs, RDP files)
# - *.cer                          (certificates)
# - NTUSER.DAT*, ntuser.*          (Windows user registry hive)
# - Desktop/, Downloads/, Pictures/, Videos/, Music/, Contacts/, Favorites/, Links/, Saved Games/, Searches/
